### Description

Initiate an approval for a fast script execution. This API only creates an approval task and runs a full pre-check on the parameters. **The script is not executed.** Once the approval is granted, Job executes it automatically as the creator of the task.

Before calling: the caller must have the permission to perform fast script execution in the target resource scope, as well as the permissions on the referenced script, execution account and target hosts. If the pre-check fails, an error is returned and no approval task is created.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| approval_channel | string | No | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel). The default channel configured on the server is used when omitted. Only the channel enum can be specified; the channel address and secret always come from the server configuration |
| task_name | string | No | Custom job name, at most 512 characters. Generated by the system when omitted |
| script_version_id | long | No | ID of the referenced script version. Provide exactly one of `script_version_id`, `script_id` and `script_content`; this one has the highest priority |
| script_id | string | No | ID of the referenced script; its online version is used. Provide exactly one of `script_version_id`, `script_id` and `script_content`; this one has the second priority |
| script_content | string | No | Base64-encoded script content. Provide exactly one of `script_version_id`, `script_id` and `script_content`; this one has the lowest priority. Script content is shown as is in the approval content so that the approver can assess the risk |
| script_language | int | No | Script language, required only when a custom script is provided via `script_content`. Options: 1 (shell), 2 (bat), 3 (perl), 4 (python), 5 (powershell), 6 (sql). Defaults to 1 |
| script_param | string | No | Base64-encoded script parameter. Note: 1. For multiple parameters such as `param1 param2`, Base64-encode `param1 param2` as a whole instead of encoding and concatenating each parameter; 2. The length before encoding cannot exceed 64K for a non-sensitive parameter and 47K for a sensitive one |
| param_sensitive | boolean | No | Whether the script parameter is sensitive. Options: `true` (sensitive, hidden on the execution detail page and shown as a placeholder in the approval content), `false` (not sensitive, the default) |
| account_alias | string | No | Alias of the execution account, usually identical to the account name on the machine, such as `root` or `user00`. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; `account_id` wins if both are given |
| account_id | long | No | ID of the execution account. Provide either `account_alias` or `account_id`; this one wins if both are given |
| windows_interpreter | string | No | Custom Windows interpreter path, must end with `.exe`, at most 260 characters |
| timeout | int | No | Script execution timeout in seconds. Defaults to 7200, valid range 1-259200 |
| execute_target | object | Yes | Execution target |
| callback_url | string | No | Callback URL invoked after the job finishes, at most 1024 characters. Job calls it once the released job completes |
| rolling_config | object | No | Rolling execution config. Rolling execution is disabled when omitted |
| start_task | boolean | No | Whether to start the job immediately after the approval is granted. Options: `true` (start immediately, the default), `false` (only create the job instance without starting it) |
| host_password_list | array | No | Custom account passwords of the target hosts. Normally not needed since the password configured in Job is used; provide it only when the hosts share the same account but have different passwords |

##### execute_target

{% include '_generic_v4_execute_target.md.j2' %}

**Note:** Hosts and containers cannot be mixed in one execution. When the target contains dynamic groups or topology nodes, the actual number of execution objects is resolved again at release time and may differ from the moment of initiation; the approval content highlights this explicitly.

{% include '_generic_rolling_config.md.j2' %}

{% include '_generic_host_password_list.md.j2' %}

**Note:** `encrypted_password` is shown as a placeholder in the approval content and never carries the real value.

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

Execute a script on hosts:

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "approval_channel": "IMATE",
    "task_name": "restart-nginx-with-approval",
    "script_content": "ZWNobyAkMQ==",
    "script_language": 1,
    "script_param": "aGVsbG8=",
    "param_sensitive": false,
    "account_alias": "root",
    "windows_interpreter": "C:\\Python38\\python.exe",
    "timeout": 1000,
    "execute_target": {
        "host_list": [
            {
                "bk_host_id": 10001
            },
            {
                "bk_cloud_id": 0,
                "ip": "127.0.0.2"
            }
        ],
        "dynamic_group_list": [
            {
                "id": "asdo8gojhasdfskft7pr5"
            }
        ],
        "topo_node_list": [
            {
                "id": 1000,
                "node_type": "module"
            }
        ]
    },
    "callback_url": "https://example.com/job/callback",
    "rolling_config": {
        "type": 1,
        "execution_mode": 1,
        "mode": 1,
        "expression": "1 5 10 100%"
    },
    "start_task": true,
    "host_password_list": [
        {
            "host_id": 10001,
            "encrypted_password": "Ug8mLwIDAQAB..."
        },
        {
            "bk_cloud_id": 0,
            "ip": "127.0.0.2",
            "encrypted_password": "Ug8mLwIDAQAB..."
        }
    ]
}
```

Execute a script in containers:

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "script_version_id": 1,
    "script_param": "aGVsbG8=",
    "param_sensitive": false,
    "account_id": 1000,
    "timeout": 1000,
    "execute_target": {
        "kube_container_filters": [
            {
                "kube_cluster_filter": {
                    "cluster_uid_list": ["BCS-K8S-00001"]
                },
                "kube_namespace_filter": {
                    "namespace_name_list": ["bkjob"]
                },
                "kube_workload_filter": {
                    "kind": "deployment",
                    "workload_name_list": ["bk-job-execute"]
                },
                "kube_pod_filter": {
                    "pod_name_list": ["bk-job-execute-0"],
                    "label_selector": [
                        {
                            "key": "app",
                            "operator": "in",
                            "values": ["bk-job-execute"]
                        }
                    ],
                    "label_selector_expr": ["app in (bk-job-execute)"]
                },
                "kube_container_prop_filter": {
                    "container_name_list": ["job-execute"]
                },
                "execute_in_whole_cluster": false
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

